cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it using these metadata."
title: "Intelligent Morphing-Wing Explorer: Physics-Informed Autonomy for Morphing Aircraft"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "Kumar Prabhakaran Saravanakumar"
repository-code: "https://github.com/kumarprabhakaransaravanakumar-wq/intelligent-morphing-wing"
url: "https://github.com/kumarprabhakaransaravanakumar-wq/intelligent-morphing-wing"
license: MIT
date-released: "2026-10-08"
abstract: >-
  Aerospace autonomy research on morphing-wing aircraft for Mars and planetary
  exploration. An opportunity optimizer selects wing geometry and trajectory
  using physics-informed prediction with learned corrections, while an
  independent risk harness and fallback controller retain safety authority.
  The project progresses from simulation to a real-world morphing-wing flight
  demonstrator to measure the sim-to-real gap.
keywords:
  - morphing wing
  - morphing aircraft
  - Mars aircraft
  - planetary exploration
  - model predictive control
  - physics-informed machine learning
  - uncertainty quantification
  - runtime assurance
  - safe autonomy
  - sim-to-real
  - system identification
  - UAV
